DESIGN GOAL:

I improved my code from the previous season. In the previous season, I gave villagers roles so that every villager was doing something. In this season, I wanted them to change their behavior depending on the time
of day.

REFLECTION:

To do this, I used behavioral blocks to give each villager a role. Since some villagers shared a role, it was easier to assign roles. In the previous seasons, I had to use time variables to make villagers
change what they were doing after some time had passed. But with the time cycle, I replaced some of those time-based variables with the time cycle.

AI DISCLOSURE:

I used Claude Code extensively in this project. The coding agent helped modify my code. After every task it completed, I checked its work by reading its new code and by testing the agent by playing
the game and looking for whether the changes were successful. Using the coding agent definitely helped with the assignment.
